    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-21T17:38:15+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-21T17:38:15+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T07:08:15Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T07:08:15Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure lingers north of the border over the Northern Territory. A slow moving high pressure system in the Tasman Sea maintains a ridge across eastern parts of the state. A trough of low pressure is forecast to move into the west on Thursday, and slowly move eastwards on Friday. Another trough and multiple cold fronts move over the state over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW008" description="Mid North" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-21T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon then becoming light in the late evening.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of fog in the early morning. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 34.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm in the south in the afternoon. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly in the middle of the day then tending southeast to southwesterly in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Light winds becoming south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching between 14 and 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
